          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life</strong><br>\nAnton Bruckner was born on September 4, 1824, in Ansfelden, Austria. Raised in a family that valued music, Bruckner learned to play the organ from an early age. He spent much of his early career as a schoolteacher and church organist, honing his skills and studying music privately in Vienna.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Religious Influence</strong><br>\nA devout Catholic, Bruckner's faith profoundly influenced his compositions. He composed numerous masses and motets, which are among his most revered works. His music often reflects his religious devotion, with compositions that include majestic organ solos and sacred choral works.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Symphonies</strong><br>\nBruckner is best known for his symphonies, which are characterized by their grand scale and use of the orchestra. These works often contain a sense of awe and spiritual contemplation, influenced by his love for the teachings of the church and the music of Richard Wagner.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Struggle for Recognition</strong><br>\nDuring his lifetime, Bruckner struggled to gain recognition, particularly for his symphonies. His works were often met with mixed reactions due to their unusual length and complexity. He revised his symphonies multiple times, which led to various versions of the same work and sometimes confusion over his intentions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Teaching and Influence</strong><br>\nBruckner was also a respected teacher, with a tenure at the Vienna Conservatory. His students included notable composers who went on to have significant careers of their own. Through his teaching, he had a considerable impact on the next generation of musicians.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Challenges</strong><br>\nBruckner's personal life was marked by difficulties, including his awkward social demeanor and lifelong bachelorhood. He often faced bouts of depression and anxiety, which affected his work and interactions with others.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
